<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA - VILNIUS BOURSE LISTS EIGHT NEW COMPANIES.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA - VILNIUS BOURSE LISTS EIGHT NEW COMPANIES.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's stock exchange said</p>
<p>on Monday that its board decided to list eight more companies</p>
<p>on its current trading list.</p>
<p>The bourse said in a statement that shares in the following</p>
<p>companies will be listed for trade on the central market and</p>
<p>block trades from May 26:</p>
<p>				     Number    Face  Total issue</p>
<p>				     of shares value in LTL</p>
<p>    - Klaipedos Konditerija  132,248   10    1,322,480</p>
<p>    - Pasidaryk Pats	   74,514     5    372,570</p>
<p>    - Apranga		    4,411,495  1    4,411,495</p>
<p>    - Stop Servis		1,581,978  1    1,581,978</p>
<p>    - Giriu Bizonas	    320,550   100   32,055,000</p>
<p>    - Kalda			1,321,482  1    1,321,482</p>
<p>    - Autoseifas		 558,492    1    558,492</p>
<p>    - Siauliu Aviacija	 701,342   10    7,013,420</p>
<p>The bourse said that all the listed share issues were</p>
<p>ordinary shares.</p>
<p>The bourse also said that the financial situation of the</p>
<p>last four companies listed on the table should be taken into</p>
<p>account since they posted losses in 1996.</p>
<p>The head of the stock exchange's listing department,</p>
<p>Saulius Malinauskas, told Reuters that 496 companies and 551</p>
<p>shares are now listed on Lithuania's market.</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
